            <ArticleTitle>A very rare congenital abnormality: double right coronary artery. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>643-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e32832ce97d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The incidence of coronary artery anomalies is about 0.6-1.3% in angiographic studies of the adult population. Double right coronary artery is one of the rarest abnormalities reported in the literature. We report a case of a double right coronary artery originating from a single orifice in a woman who underwent coronary angiography for a pathological transprosthetic aortic gradient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
